        "text": "Home\n/\nResources\n/ Chemours Titanium Dioxide Alternatives\nTechnical Evaluation Guide\nHow to Evaluate a Chemours Titanium Dioxide Alternative\n\nIf your current reference is a Chemours Ti-Pure grade, start with the exact grade, application and qualification requirements. A brand name alone is not enough to identify a suitable alternative.\n\nExplore Titanium Dioxide Products\nWhy the Exact Ti-Pure Grade Matters\n\nChemours organizes its Ti-Pure portfolio across applications including coatings, plastics and laminates, with product and application guidance for each area. When evaluating another source, the exact grade and the role it plays in your formulation or process matter.\n\nRecord the full grade name you use, along with its application and end use. These details provide a more useful basis for reviewing another titanium dioxide grade than the brand name alone.\n\nPrepare Your Evaluation Brief\n\nUse these four inputs to organize your evaluation. Start with the information you have, then add details as you review relevant product pages.\n\nCurrent reference and use.\nNote the exact Ti-Pure grade, application, formulation or system type, and end use.\nProcess and handling constraints.\nDescribe the conditions that affect how the pigment is dispersed, processed or incorporated in your system.\nPerformance and acceptance criteria.\nList the properties your application depends on, together with the test methods, target values and pass/fail criteria you use.\nDocuments required for review.\nIdentify the technical, safety, quality or origin documentation needed for your qualification process.\nCompare Documented Facts, Then Qualify the Grade\n1. Build a shortlist\n\nUse the Product Hub to find IKHLAS grades listed for your application or production process. Treat those relationships as a shortlist for review, not as replacements for your current grade.\n\n2. Compare product-specific information\n\nOpen the relevant product pages and compare documented properties with the criteria in your evaluation brief.\n\n3. Validate in your own system\n\nRun your normal formulation trials and acceptance tests before changing supply.\n\nContinue Your Evaluation\nReview IKHLAS Titanium Dioxide Grades\n\nExplore grades by application or production process, then open the relevant product pages for product-specific information.\n\nExplore Titanium Dioxide Products\nRequest Documents for a Grade You Are Evaluating\n\nIf you have selected an IKHLAS grade for review, request the TDS, SDS, COA or origin documentation you need.\n\nRequest Product Documents\nSources and Independence\n\nThe Ti-Pure portfolio and application information referenced in this guide come from the Chemours/Ti-Pure pages linked above.\n\nLast reviewed: 6 September 2026\n\nChemours and Ti-Pure are referenced only to identify the buyer's starting point. This guide is published independently by IKHLAS TITANIUM (MALAYSIA) SDN. BHD. We are not affiliated with, authorized by or endorsed by Chemours.",
        "sections": 6
